Testing is done with FRUITPy (https://github.com/acroucher/FRUITPy)

First download FRUIT https://sourceforge.net/projects/fortranxunit/
and FRUITPy.
Copy the `fruit_makefile` included in FRUITPy to fruit_3.4.1/makefile and edit the paths.
Then type
```bash
make
make install
```
You might need to copy the .mod files to your include dir yourself
(gfortran places them in the cwd while ifort places them next to the source file)

Finally you need to set FRUITPYDIR to the directory containing FRUITPy.
LIB_FRUIT and INC_FRUIT should be set to the correct library and include paths respectively.
To run the test suite, use `make test`
